--
-- demo/theGUI/hTable.exw
-- ======================
--
--  All the messy gubbins of a table in hll code, intended for testing and to
--  simplify theGUI.e ==> theGUI.js porting stage.
--
--  Note this (quite deliberately) does not have the 48-hour-lifespan 
--       gTable.ini that the otherwise equivalent gTable.exw demo has.
--  Of ourse this is the grubby longhand version, and gTable.exw has
--  the stuff just mentioned, hence see the manual for the much nicer
--  short and sweet code you probably actually want to write.
--
--  TODO: KEY handler [IN POGRESS], also:
--  Columns can also be resized by dragging the edges between column headings [FIXED]
--  Using COL_DRAG where I should be using a new COL_SIZE.. [FIXED, I think]
--  COL_DRAG: not attempted [now deliberately deferred indefinately] [FIXED]
--  Shift-click should not sort columns... but instead start COL_DRAG [FIXED]
--  dragging when not on a COL_SIZE point still does... [FIXED]
--  Ctrl-shift-click should (perhaps) reallot sizes/nick from the nearest? [DONE]
--  BUG: drag Date to zero-width, then drag Chq/Amount border fails. [NOT A BUG...]
--  rename ROW_HEIGHT as LINEHT, [done] and make it FONT-dependent [todo]
--  test ACTIVE [DONE]
--  implement TOPLINE, LINEHT, SHOWLINE
--  testme: Replacing columns automatically wipes resize_sink, and col drag/sort when not doing so would inevitably lead to a crash
--  testme: should you micro-scroll such that TOPLINE is technically 1.9, you&apos;ll just get a 1 back. (also TL is an SDX, not an RDX)
--  BUG: resize_sink still has a few glitches when columns have been reordered. [FIXED, I HOPE...]
--  No resize_sink when <=1 column. Make column dragging (both types) cancel any resize sink. Maybe...
--  BUG: widen the dialog, then double-ctrl-click Date (presumably before redraw gets in) and it goes 50-700-80. [FIXED]
--       possible new strategy: make columns {{title,min,align,act}} and get rid of actcols...
--       maybe a flag and/or factor out actcol setting so we can invoke it when it hasm'y yet been...
--  BUG: widen the dialogm and make any column a resize sink, then shrink the dialog: scrollbar kicks in, only to vanish when
--       the resize sink is deactivated - erm?? [FIXED, I think]
--
--{} = sprint(0,9) -- (set the default asCh to -1)
with javascript_semantics -- work rqd: most of the usual resize problems,
                          --           one extra blank entry from s/where
                          --           column resizers completely kaput,
                          --           CLICK_CB callback also """  """ ,
                          --           things marked as tested below were 
                          --           tested on desktop/Phix & not p2js.
--requires(`1.0.6`)
--requires(64,true)
--puts(1,``)
